You are working with the Brainbase Conversational Platform via the Mega project.

Read these docs before writing Based code or interacting with the platform:
- docs/based.md — Complete Based language reference
- docs/platform.md — Platform data model (workers, flows, deployments)
- docs/deployments.md — Deployment types and configuration
- docs/api-reference.md — Brainbase API operations, payloads, and error shapes
- examples/ — Production-quality Based flow examples

Based is Python + conversation primitives (loop/until, talk, say, ask, done, transfer).
The core pattern is: loop → talk(prompt) → until "condition" → handler code.
Keep `res = talk(...)` assignments on one physical line. Build long prompts in variables before the loop, then pass the variable to `talk()`.
Inside `until` blocks, keep `return` statements bare or as one-line `return "message"` statements. Put comments on separate lines.
Wrap API calls in try/except. Keep voice responses short.
In v2, `variables` is NOT auto-injected except when explicitly passed via `x-initial-state.variables`.

Scripts in scripts/ interact with the Brainbase API using BRAINBASE_API_KEY from .env.
GET/read-only API operations may run without extra approval. POST/PATCH/PUT/DELETE operations require explicit user approval by default.
Return API error bodies and runtime context to the agent loop so failures can be fixed and re-tested.

## Mandatory workflow

When writing or modifying flows, always follow this order:
1. Write the flow
2. Create the worker and flow
3. Test via the OAI-compatible engine (see README or CLAUDE.md "Testing flows" section) — run at least 2-3 turns
4. Fix issues found in testing, then re-test
5. Require explicit user approval before live deployment
6. Only then deploy to a live channel

Do NOT use chat deployments for testing — they are deprecated. The OAI engine is the only testing interface.
Voice deployments should pass `externalConfig.engineVersion: "v2"` explicitly even though the API may inherit worker `engineVersion`.
